1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:04,600
What happens to people who never heard of Jesus?

2
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:09,400
It is the question we are asked most — and always in a whisper.

3
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:14,600
What about those who never heard? Is it fair? What about my ancestors?

4
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:20,000
In Caesarea there lived a Roman officer, Cornelius.

5
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:24,600
A Gentile. Outside the covenant. And still, God saw him.

6
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:29,400
He feared God with all his house. He gave much to the poor. He prayed.

7
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:34,400
An angel told him: send for a man called Peter.

8
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:39,400
When Peter walked into that house, he said something that changes the question.

9
00:00:40,900 --> 00:00:44,600
God is no respecter of persons.

10
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:49,200
In every nation, the man who fears him and does right is accepted with him.

11
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:54,600
And he sent the gospel straight to the seeker.

12
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:59,400
Because no one has zero light.

13
00:01:00,200 --> 00:01:04,600
The invisible things of him are clearly seen in the things that are made.

14
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:09,600
When Paul walked through Athens, he found an altar...

15
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:14,600
...to the unknown God. Built by people reaching for a God they did not yet know.

16
00:01:15,400 --> 00:01:19,600
The third answer: God will judge every person.

17
00:01:20,600 --> 00:01:24,800
To whom much was given, much will be required.

18
00:01:25,400 --> 00:01:29,800
Centuries earlier, Abraham pleaded with God for a city.

19
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:34,800
God agreed: if even ten righteous people could be found, he would spare it.

20
00:01:36,200 --> 00:01:39,600
Ten. Not a hundred. Ten.

21
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:44,600
Mercy in judgment — the judge looking for a reason to save.

22
00:01:45,600 --> 00:01:49,600
Christians have not agreed about the unreached.

23
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:55,400
Some say: hear and trust in this life. Others say Christ may save them by a way we cannot see.

24
00:01:55,800 --> 00:01:59,800
But every one of those views agrees: salvation is only through Jesus.

25
00:02:00,400 --> 00:02:04,600
Then Paul asks a question that puts the weight on us.

26
00:02:05,400 --> 00:02:09,600
Faith comes by hearing — and hearing, by someone who was sent.

27
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:14,400
Think of the person who first told you about Jesus.
